 "text": "Hi! How are you doing? For calming bedtime story, try The Train arrives at Midnight read with musical backing. It helps the listener fall asleep the song in the background takes over. Try reading the story yourself first, so it's familiar. Then play the audio for the outro. Lots of people find their own voice soothing. I find them useful myself, but some people find them obnoxious. Try sleeping through whole night without one first. A single loud firecracker at bedtime is the trick. Grab an old firework from Fourth of July.",
